  "id": "COMPOUND:29877 - PROTEIN:5792",
  "verbalization": "Pestaloficiol A appears to interact with RWLeu4 through a series of target relationships, suggesting a potential pathway where the compound influences the activity of downstream proteins. The evidence indicates that Pestaloficiol A targets Replicase polyprotein 1ab, which in turn is targeted by Surangin D and Malvidin 3-rutinoside-5-glucoside, both of which also target RWLeu4. Similarly, Pestaloficiol A targets HPAC, which is targeted by Assafoetidnol B, which also targets RWLeu4. These findings suggest that Pestaloficiol A may act through multiple pathways, possibly by modulating different targets that ultimately converge on RWLeu4. The shared involvement of RWLeu4 across these pathways implies a potential functional role in the biological process that these compounds are targeting. The integration of these relationships highlights the complexity of the interaction network, where Pestaloficiol A may exert its effects through diverse mechanisms that ultimately lead to the activation or regulation of RWLeu4.",
